Sval: keep the granular fingerprinting overrides out of private windows

The granular-overrides prefs persist and settings sync carries them, so the
entries in them are choices made in normal windows: fingerprinting
protection off for a site, and per-site exceptions. nsRFPService kept one
map for every context, so a private window took those choices too and gave
the site real canvas, font and other values.

Each nsIFingerprintingOverride says whether it applies in private browsing.
FingerprintingWebCompatService marks the pref entries as normal-only and
Mozilla's remote webcompat entries as applying everywhere. nsRFPService
keeps a second map of the entries that apply in private browsing, so a
private context reads Mozilla's fix for a site even where a local entry
replaced it in normal windows.

No chrome API reaches this: nsIRFPService takes the entries wholesale, and
GetOverriddenFingerprintingSettingsForURI is the only place that knows
whether the context is private.

